    "narrative": "The LawDog offensive unit faces a mix of mid-tier arms today, with **Tyler Freeman** (65.30) leading the charge as our top-rated play. His score is heavily bolstered by a 14% park factor advantage and an 11% boost from facing Brady Singer, whose 4.47 xERA provides a soft landing despite a suboptimal spot in the order. Similarly, **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.78) and **Masyn Winn** (64.01) offer elite leverage due to their favorable matchups against Merrill Kelly and Michael McGreevy, respectively. **Dylan Beavers** (61.18) remains a high-upside play as he looks to exploit the matchup against P. Lambert, where his platoon advantage and batting order position provide a much-needed boost to his efficiency score.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's docket involved **Ryan Waldschmidt** (49.69), who narrowly missed the cut for the final outfield slot. While his underlying skill set is strong, the penalty for his projected ninth-order slot proved insurmountable compared to the balanced upside of **Lawrence Butler** (59.79), whose matchup against Cade Cavalli is buoyed by a significant 10% park factor and a robust 13% platoon edge. Elsewhere, our lineup remains cautious regarding **Cal Raleigh** (53.91) and **Jonathan Aranda** (50.14), both of whom are facing challenging pitchers in Landen Roupp and Bennett. We are keeping a close eye on the official lineups for **Cal Raleigh**, **Masyn Winn**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Taylor Ward**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **JJ Bleday**; any major shifts in batting order will require a reassessment of our daily caps to ensure we aren't burning limited games on sub-optimal lineup spots. \n\nWe are also benching **Luis Arraez** (45.52) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (43.03) specifically due to the matchup against Bryce Miller. While typically core components of our roster, the combination of Miller\u2019s elite 2.85 xERA and a poor park factor makes it prudent to sit them in favor of players like **Tyler Freeman** and **Geraldo Perdomo**, who benefit from much friendlier opposing arms. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Bryce Harper**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Will Smith**, **Matt Chapman**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Zack Gelof**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Drew Gilbert** as the day progresses, remaining prepared to pivot if late-breaking weather or lineup changes shift the daily efficiency landscape.",
